WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.160
H: Good Morning John!

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.100
J: Wait where do I stand? Here?

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.140
H:Yeah you know.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.220
J: I seem a little dark.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:04.860
H: I look great!

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.980
J: We switch places, I bet you'll look a little dark.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.380
H: Come on more CML! You know.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.720
J: We're here in Los Angeles together for the DFTBA.com annual meeting.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.080
H: Yeah we're talking to all the people who helped make that website work.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:22.080
J: If you need T-Shirts, posters, mugs, plushys, key-chains? Check out DFTBA.com

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.960
J: I'm a little concerned that you might be graying a little bit in the temples.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.260
J: Now I know that I am all... I'm full grey.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.300
H: You are not in any way full grey!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.980
J: I'm the oldest youtuber.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:31.640
H: No.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.420
J: I am the last living American youtuber.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.400
H:You are the last living American.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.880
H: You know a true thing John?

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:39.420
J: Yes.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.460
H: We talked about on an episode of Dear Hank &amp; John in the past, about-

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:43.960
J: That's our podcast

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:49.420
H: about how there were only two possible multiverse futures in which Donald Trump became the republican nominee.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.700
H: And in one of them...

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.860
J: We're living in the worst time I ...

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.520
H: And in one of them, it was because a meteor killed all but 12 Americans.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.300
H: But he still wasn't elected President.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:01.820
H: Alright John

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.940
H: We got some questions from people!

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.680
H: I've got questions from Snapchat.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.020
J: They "snatted" (Snapchat + Chatting) their questions?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.560
H: They "snatted" to me some questions!

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.600
J: And now we shall answer them!

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.160
H: This question is

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.260
"What is your favourite form of the potato?

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.800
J: Oh God!

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.000
J: Are we doing potatoes again?!

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.260
H: No.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.160
H: That was. I did not ask for potatoes!

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.540
H: This is completely unrelated.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.640
J: My strongly... I have a strong  preference for "French Fries".

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.580
H: The next question is

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.280
H: I don't know how to work my phone!

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.880
"Do you like snapchat filters?"

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.720
J: I'm going to level with you.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.140
J: I don't know how to use snapchat very well.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.660
J: But when I was in Jordan

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.880
J: Our interpreter "Nida" sat down with kids and used snapchat filters.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.340
J: And they were crazy about them.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.320
J: I mean they were laughing, they were screaming, they couldn't believe it.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.800
J: And then I sat down next to them

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.880
J:  And I was like, "Actually this is pretty amazing!"

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.000
H: "How cute is this cat?"

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.820
J: On a scale of like 1 to 10.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.640
J: I'm going to say 8.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.400
H: Yeah it's a pretty cute cat.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.340
H: "Who would win in a fight? Andrew Jackshon or Seodore Roosevelt?"

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.440
J: Can you just say that right?

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.580
H: "Who would win in a fight Andrew Jackshon..."

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.640
H: Who would... (laughs)

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.000
H: "Should this young woman condition or shampoo first?"

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.320
J: Oh, always shampoo then condition!

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.040
H: I never have heard of conditioning first!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.960
J: I didn't even know that conditioning first was an option!

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.940
H: You just going to wash out all the condition..ment.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:11.860
J: This nerdfighter asked ...

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.540
J: "Would vlogbrothers ever do a tour?"

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.320
H: Funny you should ask!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.020
H: Because I'm announcing "Hank and the perfect Strangers Tour" today!

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:17.520
H: Right now!

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.080
H: It's happening!

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:18.620
J: Really!

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.300
H: I just announced it!

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:19.860
J: Wow! Where you're guys all going?

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.080
H: We're going to all of these places!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.640
H: There! I didn't have to remember.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.140
J: Great!

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:24.760
H: That was great!

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.100
J: But you can also look at the link in the description about the tickets and stuff.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.800
H: Yeah all the tickets are available now

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.900
H: And they're inexpensive because we're not that popular!

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.380
J: And then Hank and I will hopefully go on tour sometime next year together.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.400
H: "What's your favourite food to eat when you're sick?"

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.800
J: You know Hank it's an old favourite, and I know a lot of people feel this way.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.800
J: But I just really enjoy "Chloraseptic Max"

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.420
H: Oh yeah, high calorie!

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.320
J: Ah, that goes right into the back of the throat, where the strep is. And it just makes it not hurt.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.780
H: It smells like a Doctor's office.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.860
H: "Favourite Taylor Swift song?"

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:51.760
J: We're going to do it on three.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.260
J: Ready?

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.200
J: 1...  2... 3!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.320
J &amp; H: Shake it off!

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.340
J: Oh my god! We should be brothers!

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.260
H: "How goes the book writing John?

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.760
J: Oh, thanks for asking, woman with angler fish!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.940
J: It's going. I'm writing.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.240
H: What word are you on?

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.260
J: Um, you mean the last word that I wrote?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.080
J: I'll look!

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.400
H: You found it?

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:10.940
J: I found the word!

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.460
J: The word is coffee

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.960
H: Ah I know a little bit about your book!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.540
J: It includes stirring milk into morning coffee, no less.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.280
H: Oh do you think that line is going to make it?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.880
J: Um - 50/50?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.960
H: All right, got another question, John...

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.260
H: "Can you show us your socks?"

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.120
J: Yes!

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.800
H: "If you were a kitchen appliance what would you be?"

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.560
J: I'd be a toaster-oven.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.220
J: You want to ask why?

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.020
H: Not really.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.360
J: Well there is really no reason. I just love toaster-ovens.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.900
H: I'd be an oven.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.280
H: Because I'm reliable, and I'm hot.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.820
H: You are reliable, hot, and inexpensive.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:48.720
J: That's right.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.720
(John coughing)

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.780
H: Very sorry, you're so sick right now.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.860
J: Oh well Hank I'll see you on ...  [coughs]

